### JavaScript
Finally, we'll use JavaScript to dynamically add the underlining effect when the page loads. Since the CSS is already providing the underline effect, we don't need any JavaScript for this specific task. However, if you need to add or remove the underlining effect dynamically, you can use JavaScript.

```javascript
